IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV: section 87 (records and books), section 88 (inspections, entry to
-- a dwelling-house, requirements to provide information, review of a judicial authorization, compliance) and section 89
-- (protection of an employer that deducts; the Minister's receipt).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- Facts the law hands to a judge or the Minister (reasonable grounds, necessity, reasonableness of a time or of assistance,
-- "considers") are BOOLEAN inputs named for the judgment; the rule answers conditionally and never guesses them.

§ `Section 87 - records and books`

-- Subsection (1): kept at the employer's place of business or residence in Canada, or at another place the Minister designates;
-- in such form and containing such information (including each insured person's Social Insurance Number) as will enable the
-- determination of premiums payable and of premiums or other amounts that should have been deducted or paid.
-- src:1395 | 87 (1) An employer paying remuneration to a person they employ in insurable employment shall keep records and books of account at the employer’s place of business or residence in Canada, or at such other place as may be designated by the Minister, in such form and containing such information, including the Social Insurance Number of each insured person, as will enable the determination of any premiums payable under this Act or any premiums or other amounts that should have been deducted or paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(1) (src:1395)
GIVEN `the records and books are kept at the employer's place of business or residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records and books are kept at another place designated by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form and information will enable the determination of any premiums payable or that should have been deducted or paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the Social Insurance Number of each insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(1) the employer has kept the records and books of account as required` IF
        (`the records and books are kept at the employer's place of business or residence in Canada` OR `the records and books are kept at another place designated by the Minister`)
    AND `the form and information will enable the determination of any premiums payable or that should have been deducted or paid`
    AND `the information includes the Social Insurance Number of each insured person`

-- Subsection (2): if the employer failed to keep adequate records, the Minister may require specified ones, and the employer
-- shall keep them.
-- src:1397 | (2) If the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account, the Minister may require the employer to keep such records and books of account as the Minister may specify, and the employer shall keep the required records and books of account.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(2) (src:1397)
GIVEN `the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has required the employer to keep the records and books of account the Minister specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(2) the employer shall keep the records and books of account the Minister specifies` IF
        `the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account`
    AND `the Minister has required the employer to keep the records and books of account the Minister specifies`

-- Subsection (3): six years after the year for which they are kept (to the end of 31 December of year Y+6), "or until written
-- permission for their prior disposal is given by the Minister": the duty ends on the day permission is given (fork F-ei3-16).
-- src:1399 | (3) The employer shall retain the records and books of account and every account and voucher necessary to verify the information contained in them for six years after the year for which they are kept, or until written permission for their prior disposal is given by the Minister.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(3) (src:1399)
GIVEN `the year for which the records, books, accounts and vouchers are kept` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(3) the employer must still retain the records and books of account` IF
        `the day in question` AT MOST (`add years` (YMD `the year for which the records, books, accounts and vouchers are kept` 12 31) 6)
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST permittedOn THEN `the day in question` LESS THAN permittedOn)

-- src:1401 | (3.1) Every employer required by this section to keep records who does so electronically shall retain them in an electronically readable format for the retention period referred to in subsection (3).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(3.1) (src:1401)
GIVEN `the employer is required by this section to keep records and does so electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are retained in an electronically readable format for the retention period referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(3.1) the employer has retained the electronic records as required` IF
    (NOT `the employer is required by this section to keep records and does so electronically`)
    OR `they are retained in an electronically readable format for the retention period referred to in subsection (3)`

-- Subsection (3.2): the Minister may, on terms and conditions acceptable to the Minister, exempt an employer or a class of
-- employers from (3.1). The exemption holds while the terms are met.
-- src:1403 | (3.2) The Minister may, on such terms and conditions as are acceptable to the Minister, exempt an employer or a class of employers from the requirement in subsection (3.1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(3.2) (src:1403)
GIVEN `the Minister has exempted the employer or a class of employers to which it belongs from the requirement in subsection (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions acceptable to the Minister are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(3.2) the employer is exempt from the requirement in subsection (3.1)` IF
        `the Minister has exempted the employer or a class of employers to which it belongs from the requirement in subsection (3.1)`
    AND `the terms and conditions acceptable to the Minister are met`

-- Subsection (4): where the employer or one of their employees is subject to a ruling under s 90 or has appealed under s 91,
-- retain everything necessary "until the ruling is made or the appeal is disposed of and any further appeal is disposed of
-- or the time for filing a further appeal has expired".
-- src:1405 | (4) If the employer or one of their employees is subject to a ruling under section 90 or has made an appeal to the Minister under section 91, the employer shall retain every record, book of account, account and voucher necessary for dealing with the ruling or the appeal until the ruling is made or the appeal is disposed of and any further appeal is disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 87(4) (src:1405)
GIVEN `the employer or one of their employees is subject to a ruling under section 90 or has made an appeal to the Minister under section 91` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ruling has been made or the appeal has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any further appeal has been disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 87(4) the employer must still retain every record, book of account, account and voucher necessary` IF
        `the employer or one of their employees is subject to a ruling under section 90 or has made an appeal to the Minister under section 91`
    AND (NOT (`the ruling has been made or the appeal has been disposed of` AND `any further appeal has been disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired`))

§ `Section 88 - inspections and requirements`

-- Subsection (1), lead-in: an authorized person, at any reasonable time and for a purpose relating to the administration or
-- enforcement of this Act, may inspect, audit or examine a document that relates or may relate to the records or books or to
-- the amount of any premium payable.
-- src:1407 | 88 (1) An authorized person may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, inspect, audit or examine any document that relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any premium payable under this Act and, for those purposes, the authorized person may
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(1) (src:1407)
GIVEN `is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any premium payable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(1) the authorized person may inspect, audit or examine the document` IF
        `is an authorized person`
    AND `acts at a reasonable time`
    AND `acts for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any premium payable under this Act`

-- Subsection (2): a dwelling-house (the keel's `s 2(1) dwelling-house`) may be entered only with the occupant's consent or
-- under a warrant issued under (3).
-- src:1411 | (2) If the premises or place is a dwelling-house, an authorized person may only enter with the consent of the occupant or under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (3).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(2) (src:1411)
GIVEN `the occupant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(2) the authorized person may enter the dwelling-house` IF
        `the occupant consents`
    OR  `the authorized person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (3)`

-- Paragraph (a): "subject to subsection (2)", enter any premises or place where records or books are or should be kept.
-- src:1407 | 88 (1) An authorized person may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, inspect, audit or examine any document that relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any premium payable under this Act and, for those purposes, the authorized person may
-- src:1408 | (a) subject to subsection (2), enter any premises or place where any records or books of account are or should be kept; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(1)(a), s 88(2) (src:1407-1408) (src:1411)
GIVEN `the authorized person may inspect, audit or examine the document under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(1)(a) the authorized person may enter the premises or place` IF
        `the authorized person may inspect, audit or examine the document under subsection (1)`
    AND `records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place`
    AND ((NOT `the premises or place is a dwelling-house`)
         OR `s 88(2) the authorized person may enter the dwelling-house` `the occupant consents` `the authorized person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (3)`)

-- Paragraph (b): the owner, occupant or person in charge must give all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions
-- relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act, and attend at the premises or place with the authorized person.
-- src:1409 | (b) require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to give the authorized person all reasonable assistance and to answer all proper questions relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act and, for that purpose, require the owner, occupant or person in charge to attend at the premises or place with the authorized person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(1)(b) (src:1409)
GIVEN `is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person is acting under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is required is reasonable assistance, an answer to a proper question relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, or attending at the premises or place with the authorized person for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(1)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give what is required` IF
        `is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place`
    AND `the authorized person is acting under subsection (1)`
    AND `what is required is reasonable assistance, an answer to a proper question relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, or attending at the premises or place with the authorized person for that purpose`

-- Subsection (3): on ex parte application by the Minister, a judge satisfied by information on oath of (a), (b) and (c) may
-- issue a warrant authorizing entry, on such conditions as the warrant specifies.
-- src:1413 | (3) If, on ex parte application by the Minister, a judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1414 | (a) there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (1),
-- src:1415 | (b) entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, and
-- src:1416 | (c) entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused,
-- src:1417 | the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(3) (src:1413-1417)
GIVEN `the Minister applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(3) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house` IF
        `the Minister applied ex parte`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (1)`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused`

-- Subsection (4): where the judge is NOT satisfied that entry is necessary, the judge may order the occupant to give reasonable
-- access to documents and make other appropriate orders, "to the extent that" access has been or may be expected to be refused
-- and the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house.
-- src:1419 | (4) If the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, the judge may
-- src:1420 | (a) order the occupant of the dwelling-house to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to any document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house, and
-- src:1421 | (b) make such other order as is appropriate in the circumstances to carry out the purposes of this Act,
-- src:1422 | to the extent that access has been or may be expected to be refused and that the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(4) (src:1419-1422)
GIVEN `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(4) the judge may order the occupant to provide access and make any other appropriate order` IF
        `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `access has been or may be expected to be refused`
    AND `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house`

-- Subsection (6): the Minister shall not impose on a "third party" a requirement under (5) relating to unnamed persons unless
-- first authorized by a judge under (7).
-- src:1428 | (6) The Minister shall not impose on any person, in this section referred to as a “third party”, a requirement under subsection (5) to provide information or any document relating to one or more unnamed persons unless the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection (7).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(6) (src:1428)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(6) the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` IF
        (NOT `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons`)
    OR  `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (7)`

-- Subsection (5): for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Part, by notice served personally or by
-- confirmed delivery service (the keel's `s 2(1) confirmed delivery service`), the Minister may require any person to provide,
-- within the reasonable time stated in the notice, information or a document, subject to (6).
-- src:1424 | (5) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to subsection (6), the Minister may for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Part, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require that any person provide, within such reasonable time as is stated in the notice,
-- src:1425 | (a) any information or additional information, including any information return or supplementary return; or
-- src:1426 | (b) any document.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(5) (src:1424-1426)
GIVEN `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states a reasonable time within which to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(5) the Minister may require the person to provide the information or document` IF
        `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Part`
    AND `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`
    AND `the notice states a reasonable time within which to provide it`
    AND `s 88(6) the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (7)`

-- Subsection (7): on ex parte application by the Minister, a judge satisfied by information on oath of (a) to (d) may authorize
-- the requirement relating to unnamed persons, on such conditions as the judge considers appropriate.
-- src:1430 | (7) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may, subject to such conditions as the judge considers appropriate, authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement under subsection (5) relating to an unnamed person or more than one unnamed person, in this section referred to as the “group”, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1431 | (a) the person or group is ascertainable;
-- src:1432 | (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Part;
-- src:1433 | (c) it is reasonable to expect, based on any grounds, including statistical or other information or past experience relating to the group or any other persons, that the person or any person in the group may have failed or may be likely to fail to provide information that is sought under the requirement or to otherwise comply with this Act; and
-- src:1434 | (d) the information or document is not otherwise more readily available.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(7) (src:1430-1434)
GIVEN `the Minister applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable to expect that the person or any person in the group may have failed or may be likely to fail to provide information that is sought under the requirement or to otherwise comply with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or document is not otherwise more readily available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(7) the judge may authorize the Minister to impose the requirement` IF
        `the Minister applied ex parte`
    AND `the person or group is ascertainable`
    AND `the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Part`
    AND `it is reasonable to expect that the person or any person in the group may have failed or may be likely to fail to provide information that is sought under the requirement or to otherwise comply with this Act`
    AND `the information or document is not otherwise more readily available`

-- src:1436 | (8) If the authorization is granted, it shall be served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (5).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(8) (src:1436)
GIVEN `the authorization is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(8) the authorization has been served as required` IF
        (NOT `the authorization is granted`)
    OR  `it is served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (5)`

-- Subsection (9): the third party served may apply for review "within 15 days after it is served" (that day counts, keel
-- fork F4), to the judge who granted it or, if that judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court.
-- src:1438 | (9) If the authorization is granted, a third party on whom it is served may, within 15 days after it is served, apply for a review of the authorization to the judge who granted it or, if the judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(9) (src:1438)
GIVEN `the applicant is a third party on whom the authorization was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the authorization was served` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the third party applies for review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(9) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` IF
        `the applicant is a third party on whom the authorization was served`
    AND `the day on which the third party applies for review` AT MOST (`the last day of` 15 `days after` `the day on which the authorization was served`)

-- Subsection (10): on the application the judge may cancel the authorization if NOT satisfied that the conditions in 7(a) to (d)
-- have been met; may confirm or vary it if satisfied that they have.
-- src:1440 | (10) On hearing the application, a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(10) (src:1440)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(10) the judge may cancel the authorization` IF
    NOT `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met`

-- src:1440 | (10) On hearing the application, a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(10) (src:1440)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(10) the judge may confirm or vary the authorization` IF
    `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) to (d) have been met`

-- src:1442 | (11) If a person is found guilty of an offence under subsection 106(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection (5), the court may make such order as it considers proper in order to enforce compliance with the requirement.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(11) (src:1442)
GIVEN `the person is found guilty of an offence under subsection 106(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(11) the court may make such order as it considers proper to enforce compliance with the requirement` IF
    `the person is found guilty of an offence under subsection 106(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection (5)`

-- src:1444 | (12) If a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section,
-- src:1445 | (a) the person by whom it is inspected, audited, or examined or to whom it is provided, or any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, may make one or more copies, or have them made; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(12)(a) (src:1444-1445)
GIVEN `a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the person by whom it is inspected, audited or examined or to whom it is provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(12)(a) the person may make one or more copies or have them made` IF
        `a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section`
    AND `is the person by whom it is inspected, audited or examined or to whom it is provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`

-- src:1444 | (12) If a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section,
-- src:1445 | (a) the person by whom it is inspected, audited, or examined or to whom it is provided, or any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, may make one or more copies, or have them made; and
-- src:1446 | (b) any document appearing to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy made under this subsection is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(12)(b) (src:1444) (src:1446)
GIVEN `a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document appears to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(12)(b) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original and has the same probative force` IF
        `a document is inspected, audited, examined or provided in accordance with this section`
    AND `the document appears to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (12)`

-- Subsection (13): no person shall hinder, molest or interfere with a person doing anything authorized by or under this
-- section, or prevent or attempt to prevent it; and every person shall, "unless the person is unable to do so", do everything
-- required by or under this section, "notwithstanding any other Act or law".
-- src:1448 | (13) No person shall hinder, molest or interfere with any person doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under this section or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing and, notwithstanding any other Act or law, every person shall, unless the person is unable to do so, do everything required by or under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 88(13) (src:1448)
GIVEN `the person hindered, molested or interfered with a person doing anything authorized by or under this section, or prevented or attempted to prevent a person from doing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did everything required of them by or under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 88(13) the person has complied with the subsection` IF
        (NOT `the person hindered, molested or interfered with a person doing anything authorized by or under this section, or prevented or attempted to prevent a person from doing it`)
    AND (`the person did everything required of them by or under this section` OR `the person was unable to do so`)

§ `Section 89 - protection of the employer that deducts`

-- Subsection (1): "No action lies against any person for deducting a sum of money in compliance or intended compliance with this
-- Act." For a deduction not made in compliance or intended compliance the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1450 | 89 (1) No action lies against any person for deducting a sum of money in compliance or intended compliance with this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 89(1) (src:1450)
GIVEN `the sum was deducted in compliance or intended compliance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 89(1) an action lies against the person for deducting the sum` IS
    IF `the sum was deducted in compliance or intended compliance with this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (2): the Minister's receipt for an amount deducted as required is "a good and sufficient discharge of the
-- liability of any debtor to their creditor with respect to the deduction to the extent of the amount mentioned in the receipt".
-- src:1452 | (2) The Minister’s receipt for an amount deducted by a person as required by or under this Act is a good and sufficient discharge of the liability of any debtor to their creditor with respect to the deduction to the extent of the amount mentioned in the receipt.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 89(2) (src:1452)
GIVEN `the amount was deducted by a person as required by or under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister gave a receipt for the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount mentioned in the receipt` IS A NUMBER
      `the debtor's liability to their creditor with respect to the deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 89(2) the amount of the debtor's liability that is discharged` IS
    IF `the amount was deducted by a person as required by or under this Act` AND `the Minister gave a receipt for the amount`
    THEN JUST (IF `the amount mentioned in the receipt` LESS THAN `the debtor's liability to their creditor with respect to the deduction`
               THEN `the amount mentioned in the receipt`
               ELSE `the debtor's liability to their creditor with respect to the deduction`)
    ELSE NOTHING
